    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0283" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/8–944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-10T18:00:00-04:00">August 10, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6318. Please take no action on my telegram of August 9<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d143-f1"/> authorizing you to inform the British and Soviet
                    representatives on E.A.C. of our intention to communicate the surrender terms to
                    the Chinese. We are taking this matter up with the President and shall
                    communicate with you later.</p>
                <p>In view of the information set forth in your 6370 of August 9, if the Chinese are
                    informed of the surrender terms it will be done in such manner as to maintain
                    complete security. If the President approves, we contemplate communicating
                    orally to the Chinese only the substance of the terms on the understanding that
                    they will not be transmitted to Chungking by cable or by pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
